<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>About | Bakor Hospital prototype</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/bkh.css"></head><body class="bkh-app"><main class="bkh-page bkh-narrow"><a class="bkh-logo" href="/login"><span class="bkh-logo-mark" aria-hidden="true">B</span><span class="bkh-logo-copy"><strong>Bakor</strong><small>HOSPITAL</small></span></a><h1 class="bkh-about-heading">About this prototype</h1><div class="bkh-about-copy"><p>This is an independent academic prototype for a case study. It is not affiliated with Bakor Hospital. All patients, staff, drugs and figures are fictional.</p><p>This is not a certified clinical system. Do not use it for real patient care or real patient data. Clinicians make all clinical decisions. There is no automated diagnosis, telemedicine, video or chat; appointments are in person.</p><p>Payments are record-keeping only. The source does not specify a payment gateway or HMO/insurance module. Laboratory and pharmacy/inventory are included to meet the objectives and DFD scope. Nurses are not modeled; doctors record vitals.</p><p>The schema is original because the case study does not define a field-level schema. Reports are descriptive statistics only. Health data is sensitive: the prototype includes access control and encryption helpers, but not every privacy workflow in the specification. This is not a legal compliance certification.</p><p>Deployment to a cloud VM behind HTTPS is a deployment option; no real deployment was performed. This implementation is an educational starting point and does not implement every workflow in the full specification.</p></div><a href="/login">Return to sign in</a></main></body></html>
